# colors() from the softcode audit (#2268): every conversion PennMUSH's help shows, plus the other
# formats, background colours, xterm numbers and the errors.
::case colors.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case colors.help  the examples in help colors2
think colors(*yellow*)
think colors(+yellow, hex)
think colors(+yellow, xterm256)
think colors(+yellow, 16color)
think colors(/+yellow, 16color)
think colors(#ffff00, name)
think colors(iuB+red, hex styles)
think colors(+blue huyG/+black, auto)

::case colors.formats  each format and its short name
think colors(+orange, rgb)
think colors(+orange, r)
think colors(+orange, d)
think colors(+orange, h)
think colors(+orange, c)
think colors(+orange, x)
think colors(+lightyellow, auto)
think colors(hr, hex)
think colors(r, hex)
think colors(hr, 16color)
think colors(R, 16color)
think colors(+xterm200, 16color)
think colors(+xterm200, hex)
think colors(200, xterm256x)
think colors(0xff, d)
think colors(0xabc, hex)
think colors(<255 128 0>, hex)
think colors(<#123456>, xterm256)
think colors(#123456, 16color)
think colors(#123456, name)
think colors(+red/+blue, hex)
think colors(+red/+blue, 16color)
think colors(+red/+blue, auto)
think colors(fhu+red, styles 16color)
think colors(h, styles)

::case colors.errors  the errors
think colors(+nosuchcolor, hex)
think colors(n, hex)
think colors(+red, bogus)
think colors(#12345, hex)
think colors(+red,)
think words(colors())
think colors(xterm1*)
